  "aiOverview": {
    "content": "\"Fourth\" refers to the ordinal number (4th) following third, and is also the name of a leading AI-powered software platform for hospitality/retail workforce and inventory management. It signifies a position in a sequence, a quarter of a whole, or a, in music, an interval. Fourth (Technology Company): A global provider of intelligent, data-driven solutions for restaurants, hotels, and retailers to manage inventory, workforce, and payroll. Fourth Amendment (U.S. Constitution): Protects citizens against \"unreasonable searches and seizures\" by the government and requires warrants for, in most cases, searches to be supported by probable cause. Fourth Estate (Politics/Government): A term for the press or media, which is considered a watchdog that influences politics and government, often operating outside the direct three branches. Fourth of July: Independence Day in the United States, celebrating the adoption of the Declaration of Independence in 1776. Note: \"Fourth\" (position) is distinct from \"forth\" (forward in time or place).",
